DO $$
DECLARE
  _body text := $body$OWNER AND RENTER AGREEMENT

Agreement Date: {{agreement_date}}
Region: {{region}}

{{owner_full_name}}, of {{owner_address}}, known as "OWNER",
AND
{{driver_full_name}}, of {{driver_address}}, {{driver_city}}, {{driver_state_zip}}, known as "DRIVER".
Collectively, all of the above people or businesses entering this Agreement will be referred to as the Parties.

PURPOSE OF THE AGREEMENT
OWNER wishes to rent a personal vehicle to DRIVER, and DRIVER wishes to rent from OWNER, on the online platform {{platform_entity}}, subject to the terms and conditions of this Agreement.

Vehicle (make, model and year): {{vehicle_make_model_year}}
Vehicle Identification Number: {{vehicle_vin}}
Colour: {{vehicle_color}}
Licence Plate: {{license_plate}}
Together with all its equipment, tools, tires, accessories, keys and documents (the "Vehicle").
Previous mileage: {{previous_mileage}} | Present mileage: {{present_mileage}} (photographs to be taken at handover).

THIS CONTRACT TERMINATES EVERY 24 HOURS OF DRIVING WITHOUT PAYMENT THEREAFTER, EITHER DAILY OR WEEKLY. THE VEHICLE SHOULD BE RETURNED DIRECTLY TO THE OWNER/AGENT IN GOOD CONDITION, FAILURE OF WHICH WILL BE REPORTED TO THE RENTER'S REFEREES FOR POSSIBLE ASSISTANCE TO RECOVER. THE CAR MAY BE REPORTED TO LAW ENFORCEMENT AS THEFT ("UNAUTHORIZED USE OF PROPERTY").
NO SMOKING IN THE CAR PLEASE.

{{platform_entity}} is a third party, free market platform which facilitates transactions between car owners and car drivers by providing a platform for Owners to list one or more vehicles for rent and for Drivers to find a suitable vehicle to rent for private or commercial purposes. {{platform_entity}} is not a party to any transaction or to this Agreement between the Parties.

1. TERM
Contract start date: {{contract_start_date}} at {{contract_start_time}}
Contract end date: {{contract_end_date}} at {{contract_end_time}}

2. PAYMENTS
Basic car rental price for the booking: {{currency}} {{basic_rental_price}} (20% platform fees apply for admin; daily pay attracts a 10% surcharge).
Negotiation reference: {{negotiation_id}}
2.1. In case of any rental extension(s), this contract will be valid as long as payments are made, or until the Vehicle is returned to the Owner, whichever is earlier. This contract will be valid as per applicable laws.
2.2. If the rental period is not extended and the Vehicle is not returned within 72 hours (or such other time as required by contract) of the end of the term defined in Section 1 above, the Vehicle may be reported as stolen and the Renter held liable for all associated recovery fees and other costs.
2.3. Renter shall pay all other charges due in accordance with this Agreement upon return of the Vehicle, to the fullest extent allowed by law, including but not limited to:
a) Charges for optional services, if any;
b) Applicable taxes;
c) Mileage driven: occasional travel beyond the rideshare coverage area or DMV jurisdiction must be to the knowledge and approval of the Owner. Mileage driven is unlimited up to {{weekly_mileage_limit}} for this Vehicle, and an additional fee of {{currency}} {{excess_mileage_fee}} applies for excess (extra mileage assessed weekly);
d) Loss of, damage to, or repair of the Vehicle, loss of use, and diminution of the Vehicle's value caused by damage to or repair of it, and costs to recover such charges including administrative fees for claim processing and legal expenses; additionally the Renter authorizes the Owner to charge against the Renter's payment method on file;
e) Daily rent plus an additional 10% late delivery admin fee, payable to {{platform_entity}}, beginning the second day that payment is not made or the car is not delivered timely as per Section 1 above; alternatively the car may be disabled;
f) Unless due to the fault of the Owner, all fines, penalties, traffic and/or parking violations, toll fees, court costs, towing and impound charges, and other expenses relating to the Vehicle assessed against the Owner or the Vehicle during the rental term, shall be paid by the Renter within 72 hours of notice;
g) All expenses the Owner incurs related to the Renter's failure to return the Vehicle, including but not limited to the costs of locating and recovering the Vehicle;
h) 1.5% interest per month, or the maximum amount allowed by law, for any monies owed which are more than 14 days past due;
i) All costs incurred to collect unpaid monies due; and
j) Twenty-five dollars ($25.00) or the maximum amount allowed by law, whichever is greater, if the Renter's payments are stopped, rejected for non-sufficient funds, or dishonoured for any other reason.

3. LOSS OF COMMUNICATION (NOT PICKING CALLS)
If the Renter does not extend the rental term of the Vehicle or does not timely communicate (pick calls) with the Owner or {{platform_entity}}, the Vehicle is assumed to be lost after three (3) days and could be reported as stolen. {{platform_entity}} will also report the loss to the appropriate law enforcement agency, to one or more credit reporting services, and cause the loss to be entered into one or more national databases. Only those who are a Party to this Agreement and hold a current, valid driver's licence to operate an automobile are permitted to drive the Vehicle. Any other drivers are prohibited from operating the Vehicle, and should any such person drive the Vehicle, even if it is stolen or lost, the Renter remains liable for all such activity and resulting losses or damages.

4. INSURANCE
Loss or damage to the car and passengers, including all medical expenses, will be covered by the Transportation Network Company (Uber, Lyft or others) insurance account. The Owner must have insurance on the Vehicle as well (a requirement in most states). The Renter's insurance does NOT replace an Owner's requirement to maintain personal or other insurance as required by law. Insurance coverage starts at the exact date and time of the rental contract start and end times as defined in Section 1 above. By submitting your driver's licence you agree that {{platform_entity}} or its partners may facilitate insurance through a reputable insurance company using your information at our disposal.

5. RESTRICTION OF USE
The Renter shall not:
a) Permit the Vehicle to be driven by any person who is not an Authorized Driver under this Agreement;
b) Operate the Vehicle or permit it to be operated in violation of law, including, but not limited to, driving under the influence of alcohol or drugs, or in breach of any rules or regulations of road traffic;
c) Operate the Vehicle or permit it to be operated to commit any violation of law;
d) Operate the Vehicle or permit it to be operated for any race, test or contest;
e) Operate the Vehicle or permit it to be operated for the transport of more passengers or goods than the maximum allowable for the Vehicle, or to carry hazardous materials or explosive substances of any kind;
f) Drive or permit the Vehicle to be driven by any person who does not hold a current valid driver's licence to operate an automobile;
g) Drive or permit the Vehicle to be driven or parked on roadways not regularly maintained, or on any roads, beaches, driveways or surfaces likely to cause damage to the Vehicle;
h) Drive or permit the Vehicle to be driven or parked in areas known to have high crime rates, and/or park the Vehicle in locations where the Renter knows or should know it is likely to be stolen;
i) Operate the Vehicle or allow it to be operated to push or tow any other vehicle;
j) Transport any animal in the Vehicle (with the exception of certified or licensed animals assisting persons with disabilities); and/or
k) Allow any person to smoke and/or take or use illicit drugs in the Vehicle;
l) Travel beyond the rideshare jurisdiction or DMV without the knowledge and approval of the Owner. The Owner may reject travel on the condition of excess mileage (Section 2.3(c) refers).

6. REPAIR, LOSS AND REPORTING TO POLICE
The Owner shall reimburse the Driver for the cost of oil changes and all other repairs. The Vehicle shall not be serviced or repaired, and parts and accessories shall not be replaced, without the Owner's prior written (SMS allowed) consent. The Renter shall alert the Owner and {{platform_entity}} to any damage to or loss of the Vehicle. The Renter shall be responsible for any loss or damage to the Vehicle, loss of use, diminution of the Vehicle's value caused by damage or repair to it, and for any and all missing equipment. In the event the Renter is in an accident, has an incident in the Vehicle, or if the Vehicle is subject to theft or vandalism, the Renter shall immediately report the accident or incident to the Owner or {{platform_entity}}. In the event the Vehicle is stolen, the Renter shall immediately report the incident to local law enforcement, to the Owner and to the {{platform_entity}} platform ({{support_email}}, {{support_phone}}). The Renter agrees to pay $500 for lost, unreturned keys.

7. CONDITION OF VEHICLE
The Owner acknowledges that the Renter has examined the Vehicle (photographing existing dents) and that it is in good condition. Upon return of the Vehicle, scratches and minor damage are considered wear and tear and may not be reported to any insurance company unless wider than one foot and deeper into the paint.

8. RETURN OF VEHICLE
The Renter shall return the Vehicle on the date and at the time specified in Section 1 above, in the same condition as the Renter received it, except for normal wear and tear, and to the agreed return location. If the Vehicle is not returned on said date and at said time, the Owner reserves the right to take any legal action necessary to regain possession of the Vehicle, including reporting the Vehicle as stolen to the appropriate law enforcement organizations.

9. TERMINATION
This Agreement shall terminate on the date specified in Section 1. The Owner reserves the right to terminate this Agreement earlier upon five (5) days' notice to the Renter. The Driver should notify the Owner of a non-performing vehicle within 72 hours and return it or have it fixed. When drivers terminate earlier than the contract end date, other than through the fault of the Owner or a mechanical issue, the security deposit is deemed forfeited.

10. OWNERSHIP
The Owner shall at all times retain ownership of and title to the Vehicle. The Renter shall immediately notify the Owner in the event the Vehicle is levied, has a lien attached, or is threatened with lien and/or seizure as a result of the Renter's action, inaction, possession or use of the Vehicle. The Renter shall indemnify and hold the Owner harmless against any and all losses and/or damages caused by such action or inaction.

11. PLATFORM ROLE
{{platform_entity}} is a third party, free market platform which facilitates transactions between car owners and car drivers. {{platform_entity}} does not own any vehicles nor is it responsible for any actions caused by any Renter and/or Owner. As such, both the Owner and the Renter waive any and all actual or potential claims against {{platform_entity}} on any grounds, including, but not limited to, indemnity or claims arising out of any lawsuit or other form of damages.

12. SEVERABILITY
In the event any provision of this Agreement is held by a court or other tribunal of competent jurisdiction to be unenforceable, that provision will be enforced to the maximum extent permissible under applicable law, and the other provisions of this Agreement will remain in full force and effect. Upon a determination that any term or other provision is invalid or illegal and is material to this Agreement, the parties shall negotiate in good faith to modify this Agreement so as to effect the original intent of the parties as closely as possible.

13. ENTIRE AGREEMENT
This Agreement represents the entire understanding relating to the subject matter hereof and prevails over any prior or contemporaneous, conflicting or additional communications. This Agreement can only be modified by a written amendment signed by the parties.

14. ASSIGNMENT
The Renter may not, without the prior written consent of the Owner, transfer or assign this Agreement or any part thereof. Any attempt to do so shall be a material breach of this Agreement and shall render this Agreement void.

15. HEADINGS
The section headings used in this Agreement are for reference only and shall not be used or relied upon in the interpretation of this Agreement.

16. COUNTERPARTS
This Agreement, and any amendment thereof, may be executed in two or more counterparts, each of which shall be deemed an original, but all of which together shall constitute one and the same document.

17. CONSENT TO CONTACT
The Renter authorizes and consents to the Owner and {{platform_entity}} from time to time contacting the Renter and the Renter's referees Monday through Sunday by telephone call by any live person or entirely pre-recorded message to any landline or cellular telephone number provided or identified on record as belonging to the Renter. These live or entirely pre-recorded messages include messages previously recorded by a live person, "robo calls" and drop-in voice messages. The Renter further authorizes and consents to communications by email, text message, SMS, letter and/or facsimile to any private facsimile line identified to the Owner and/or {{platform_entity}}. The Renter also agrees that any such contact through these methods may be made 24 hours daily, and that, with no limitation on the time, length or duration, the Owner or {{platform_entity}} may from time to time contact the Renter or the Renter's referees/guarantors.

18. APPLICABLE TAXES
Owners and Renters shall be responsible to pay applicable taxes by themselves according to federal and state laws. Hence {{platform_entity}} does not charge taxes on transactions.

19. STATUTE OF LIMITATION
The Renter agrees to waive and fully give up any right to claim that any debt(s) owed under this Agreement is/are not collectable by reason of any statute of limitations.

20. OBLIGATION TO UPDATE CONTACT INFORMATION
The Renter agrees to update any information submitted to the Owner in accordance with the Renter's obligations, including but not limited to any changes in employment, spouse's employment, residence, spouse's residence, and other similar contact information as requested by the Owner, or any such information for any guarantors in this Agreement. The Renter authorizes the Owner and {{platform_entity}} to from time to time contact the Renter, the Renter's spouse and any known relatives (referees) regarding such information to request such updates.

21. ELECTRONIC SERVICE
The Renter agrees and consents to service of any process, including formal legal process in any legal proceedings, by electronic service, including email, private facsimile and any other forms of electronic communication to any contact point the Renter provides to the Owner or {{platform_entity}}. The Renter agrees to deem any service by electronic means to be the same as personal service.

22. CREDIT REPORT AND BACKGROUND CHECK
The Renter authorizes the Owner and {{platform_entity}} and agrees that, regardless of any statute, {{platform_entity}} may from time to time obtain any consumer credit report and background check deemed reasonably necessary in order to confirm the financial ability and moral reputability of the Renter to enter into this Agreement and rent a car.

The Renter acknowledges receipt of a copy of this Agreement and acknowledges having read and understood the foregoing.

BOTH YOU AND {{platform_entity}} AGREE TO RESOLVE ALL DISPUTES THROUGH BINDING INDIVIDUAL ARBITRATION. BINDING INDIVIDUAL ARBITRATION MEANS THAT YOU AND RENTMAIKAR ARE EACH WAIVING THE RIGHT TO A JURY TRIAL OR TO PARTICIPATE IN A CLASS ACTION IN THE EVENT OF A DISPUTE.

NO SMOKING IN THE CAR PLEASE.

EXECUTION
{{owner_full_name}} ({{owner_email}}), known as "OWNER" - signature and date captured electronically on the RentMaiKar platform.
{{driver_full_name}} ({{driver_email}}), known as "DRIVER" - signature and date captured electronically on the RentMaiKar platform.
Witnessed for {{platform_entity}} by the RentMaiKar Administrator - administrator signature and date captured electronically on the RentMaiKar platform.
$body$;
BEGIN
  UPDATE public.legal_agreement_templates
     SET is_active = false, updated_at = now()
   WHERE agreement_type = 'vehicle_rental'
     AND region IN ('USA','Nigeria')
     AND is_active = true;

  INSERT INTO public.legal_agreement_templates
    (template_key, agreement_type, region, title, version, content, is_active)
  VALUES
    ('owner_driver_agreement', 'vehicle_rental', 'USA', 'Owner and Driver Rental Agreement - USA', '2.0', _body, true),
    ('owner_driver_agreement', 'vehicle_rental', 'Nigeria', 'Owner and Driver Rental Agreement - Nigeria', '2.0', _body, true);
END $$;